You are executing the saas-customer-success-playbook skill. Mandate: produce Customer_Success_Playbook.md.

1. Read PRD.md, Pricing_And_Packaging_Spec.md, Onboarding_Journey_Spec.md (if available), churn data, contract types.
2. Define Customer Health Score: composite signals (usage depth, breadth, engagement frequency, support sentiment, NPS, contract age, expansion signal), weights, scoring formula, refresh cadence (weekly), bands (Green/Yellow/Red), action per band.
3. Segment customers by tier × stage. Stages: onboarding 0-90d, adoption 90-365d, renewal window T-90 to T-0, at-risk, churned-recoverable.
4. Write per (segment, stage) plays. Each play: Trigger, Owner, Action, Channels, Frequency, Success measurement, Escalation rule. Minimum plays: Onboarding kickoff (D0), First-value milestone (D7), 30-day health review, At-risk intervention, Renewal forecast T-90/T-60/T-30, Renewal-at-risk save, Expansion/upsell, Dunning recovery, Churned-recoverable re-engagement.
5. Write QBR template: business objectives, usage review, value delivered, support summary, expansion opportunities, action items.
6. Define escalation matrix: triggers for escalating CSM → CS Lead → CRO → executive sponsor.
7. Document tooling (CRM, CS platform, billing) and the source-of-truth.
8. Define cadence and review (weekly health review, monthly business review, quarterly playbook revision).
9. Write Customer_Success_Playbook.md.

Validation: Halt if any play lacks trigger or owner. Halt if Health Score lacks formula or refresh cadence. Halt if dunning recovery play is missing.
